            <ArticleTitle>Atropine Eye Drops: A Proposed Field Expedient Substitute in the Absence of Atropine Autoinjectors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nerve agents are a threat to military and civilian health. The antidote, atropine sulfate, is delivered by autoinjector, which is a limited resource. We propose the use of 1% atropine ophthalmic solution (supplied commercially in 5mL or 15 mL bottles) via oral, ocular, and intranasal administration as an expedient substitute in austere environments.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2017.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
